    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32231" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏcŭlārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the eyes</i>, <i>eye-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">CHIRVRGVS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 400, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">claritas,</span>”
				<i>of the eyes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 24, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aegritudo,</span>”
				<i>a disease of the eyes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ocularius medicus,</span>”
				<i>an oculist</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					6, 6, 8</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏcŭlārĭus</span></b> ,
				i, m., <i>an
			oculist</i>, <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 37</span></i>.</div>
